# Only what the server needs to run, named one by one. Everything else stays
# out — including whatever lands in the checkout later. A list of what to leave
# out let an agent's 7 GB working folder, recordings included, into the image;
# an image is the thing that gets published, so the safe default is "not in".
#
# The licence boundary is part of this: no client, no assets, no compatibility
# data, no captures. local-data/, content/ and game-data/ are supplied at run
# time from a copy the operator may use.
*

!src/
# Modes a deployment may load with ODS_MODES: code only, written against the mode surface.
!examples/
!config/
!db/
!tools/
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.env.example
!LICENSE
!NOTICE.md
!README.md

# Inside those, what a deployment or a developer keeps for itself (all of it
# also in .gitignore).
config/content-packs.json
config/floors.*.json
tools/client-patches/
